LALABASE — PERSONAL DATA EXPORT (Art. 15 / Art. 20 GDPR)
=========================================================

Generated at: <%= l(generated_at, format: :long) %>
Account: <%= user.email %>
Format version: 1

CONTENTS OF THIS ARCHIVE
------------------------
This archive contains the personal data Lalabase processes about your user
account, as machine-readable JSON files:

  account.json                    Your account master data
  preferences.json                Your personal settings
  memberships.json                Your organisation memberships and roles
  security_history.json           Login and security events (incl. IP addresses)
  api_tokens.json                 Metadata of your API tokens (never the tokens themselves)
  notification_preferences.json   Your notification settings
  organisations/<name>/…          Per organisation: your time tracking, private
                                  to-dos, e-mail history (metadata) and an
                                  inventory of the content you created
                                  (titles and dates, no full texts)

CONTENT INSIDE ORGANISATIONS
----------------------------
For content inside an organisation (tickets, notes, documents) the respective
organisation is the data controller; Lalabase acts as a processor. This
archive therefore contains an inventory of your own contributions in
organisations you are or were a member of (while the membership exists). For
content in organisations you were removed from, please contact the
administrator of that organisation.

YOUR RIGHTS
-----------
Access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction
(Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), objection (Art. 21). You can delete
your account yourself at any time in the account settings.

<% if privacy_link.present? %>
Details on purposes, recipients, processors and retention periods are always
up to date in the privacy policy:
<%= privacy_link %>
<% end %>

ABOUT THIS FILE
---------------
The download link for this archive is valid for 7 days; after that the file
is deleted automatically. Store the archive safely — it contains all of the
data listed above in plain text.
